  "name": "Folklore Clinical Variant Interpretation MCP",
  "alternateName": [
    "folklore-mcp"
  ],
  "description": "MCP server exposing source-linked GRCh38 germline variant interpretation to LLM agents — automated ACMG/AMP classification, gene profiles, and supporting scientific literature. The Apache-2.0 adapter in the repository implements MCP transport, public API clients, and response projection (11 anonymous tools, 18 more with an API key), and can be run locally or via Docker. Important: the variant classification itself runs on Helena Bioinformatics' hosted Folklore service (api.helena.bio), not in the open repository — so the core interpretation logic is a proprietary hosted service. The server accepts no patient or case context and states that outputs require qualified professional review.",
  "url": "https://folklore.helena.bio",
